 per Cell\n\n| Grade | Region A | Region B | Region C | Region D |\n|-------|----------|----------|----------|----------|\n| G10 | 83.2759 | 81.0400 | 81.5172 | 81.1429 |\n| G11 | 80.9375 | 83.9143 | 80.4524 | 80.7895 |\n| G12 | 79.5000 | 79.6452 | 79.3429 | 79.9000 |\n\nEach cell value is the arithmetic mean of `reading_score` for students in that grade/region combination (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean per cell; sample sizes as listed in Table 2.1).\n\n### 2.3 Full Cell Detail (Count + Mean)\n\n| Grade | Region | Row Count (n) | Mean `reading_score` |\n|-------|--------|---------------|----------------------|\n| G10 | A | 29 | 83.2759 |\n| G10 | B | 25 | 81.0400 |\n| G10 | C | 29 | 81.5172 |\n| G10 | D | 42 | 81.1429 |\n| G11 | A | 32 | 80.9375 |\n| G11 | B | 35 | 83.9143 |\n| G11 | C | 42 | 80.4524 |\n| G11 | D | 38 | 80.7895 |\n| G12 | A | 32 | 79.5000 |\n| G12 | B | 31 | 79.6452 |\n| G12 | C | 35 | 79.3429 |\n| G12 | D | 30 | 79.9000 |\n\nRow counts: (Source: offline_data/students.csv `grade`/`region`, count & n per cell). Means: (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean & n per cell).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n\n- **Highest mean combination:** G11 × Region B, mean = 83.9143 (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean & n=35).\n- **Lowest mean combination:** G12 × Region C, mean = 79.3429 (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean & n=35).\n- **Spread between highest and lowest cell means:** 4.5714 points (Source: calculated from previous rows).\n\n## 4. Conclusion\n\nAcross the 400 students (Source: offline_data/students.csv, row count & n=400), reading performance varies modestly by grade and region. The G11 students in Region B achieve the highest mean reading score of 83.9143 (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean & n=35), while the G12 students in Region C record the lowest mean of 79.3429 (Source: offline_data/students.csv `reading_score`, mean & n=35). The gap between these